# some_motion: "motion" in S2 is motion evident to the senses, while S4 defines motion broadly as reduction from potentiality to actuality. Sensible motion is a case of that broader sense, not a different one, so the claim is in one sense.
# first_mover / infinite_regress: the hand-and-staff example in S12 suggests "first" means first in an ordered series of causes, not first in time. Every statement that uses these claims reads them that way, so I marked them one.
